{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Plug-in", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about plug \u2013ins.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about plug\u2013ins. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Define plug\u2013ins in a paragraph of five lines. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use simple past tense to talk about plug-ins history.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your paragraph. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your work with two classmates.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for information about plug\u2013ins. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I define plug\u2013ins in a paragraph of five lines. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use simple past tense. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about plug-ins and its features.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "advertisement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a paid announcement that promotes a product or a service", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Whenever I opened the web browser, tons of advertisement appeared and it made the computer kind of slow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "personalize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give a specific, unique or own style to something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are some plug-ins that let users personalize their accounts on some social networks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "blocker", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a program that stops and eliminates unwanted things from your browser", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you install any advertisement blocker plug-in?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "developers", "type": "name"}, {"content": "experts in software programming", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many computer application let third party developers write little programs that add different functions to them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "plug-in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "small piece of software that provides web browser compatibility", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you install any advertisement blocker plug-in?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "essential", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is really important", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you know some plug-ins are essential if you want?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<strong>Simple Past: Auxiliary Be vs Auxiliary Did in Questions and Negative</strong>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <b>simple past</b> to talk about finished actions in the past. Let's see how to use verb to <b>be</b> and the auxiliary <b>did</b> in the interrogative and negative forms. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Let's check how both <strong><i>did</i></strong> and <strong><i>to be</i></strong> works in past to express question and negative sentences.</br></br>  <div align=\"center\"><strong>Verb to Be in Simple Past</strong></div></br></br>  <strong>Questions</strong></br> To ask about past events or actions in close questions follow this structure:</br> <center><strong>Was/Were</strong> + subject + complement + ?</center></br> Examples:</br> <i><strong>Was</strong> the computer on?</br> <strong>Were</strong> you concerned about the issue?</i></br></br>  <strong>Negative</strong></br> To make negative statements about past use:</br><center> Subject + <strong>was/were</strong> + <strong>not</strong> + complement.</center></br>  Examples:</br> <i>The plug-in <strong>was not</strong> installed.</br> They <strong>were not</strong> sure about the reason of the problem.</i></br></br>  <strong>*Contractions</strong></br> <i>Was not = wasn't</br> We're not = weren't</i></br>  <strong><br><center>Auxiliary Verb Did</center></strong></br> In order to make close questions with verbs that are different from the verb to be follow this structure:</br><br><b> Questions</b></br> <strong>Did</strong> + subject + verb in base form + complement?</br>  Examples:</br> <i><strong>Did</strong> you use any plug-in?</i></br></br>  <strong>Negative:</strong></br> Subject + <strong>did + not</strong> + verb in base form + complement</br> Examples</br> <i>I <strong>did not</strong> understand what a plug-in is.</i></br>  <strong><br>**Contraction</strong></br> <strong>Did  + not = didn't</strong></br></br>  Remember if you want to ask about specific information you should add a Wh question word at the beginning of the questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Did you know some plug-ins are essential if you want? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did you install any advertisement blocker plug-in?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<strong>Wh-Questions</strong>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use <b>WH-questions</b>, you ask for specific information; so we cannot answer this kind of questions using yes or not, but giving specific details. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<div align=\"center\"><strong>Wh-Questions Structure</strong></div></br></br> You create WH-questions adding a WH-word  or interrogative adverb to the structure of a question. </br></br> <center>  <strong>Wh-Word</strong> + auxiliary verb + subject + main verb + complement +?</center></br></br>  Look at the following chart to check the most common interrogative adverbs:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Wh-Word</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Purpose </strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Chooses something within a variety of things.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Why\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks for a reason.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks for a place.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks for a specific moment.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks for a specific someone.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"How\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks for the way in which something happens.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks to choose something within a limited number of options.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "How can I help you today? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What kind of functions?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Popular Plug-Ins to Build Your Own Web Page", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<b>Plug-ins</b> are small programs that can widen the features of other programs that are commonly bigger. The most common examples are the web browsers and their extension.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The following chart shows some popular plug-ins:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Plug-ins</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Functionality </strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wordfence Security\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Provides security to your website.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"WP-PageNAvi\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adds a more advanced page navigation experience.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disable Comments\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disables the comments section easily.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"WP Smush - Image Optimization\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It allows you to reduce the size of images while improving page performance\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"TablePress\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adds tables and chats to you page\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"WP Maintenance Mode\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It allows visitors know your site is down for maintenance.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bbPress\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It gives you the opportunity to create a forum.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Gallery\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adds a photo gallery to your page.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Easy Google Fonts\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adds Google fonts easy and without codex.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can explain what a plug-in is. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can understand why plug-ins are required. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify information and concepts related to plug - ins.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What features can you find in a web browser?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "In your opinion, how can we improve the performance of a web browser?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback